# MarkUP showcase

MarkUP is **Markdown with components**. Everything you know from Markdown works —
*emphasis*, `code`, [links](https://github.com), ~~strikethrough~~ and footnotes[^why] —
and components add structure where plain Markdown runs out. :badge[v0.1]{variant=info}

::toc[On this page]{depth=3}

## Callouts

:::note
Callouts highlight information. There are five kinds: `note`, `tip`, `important`, `warning` and `caution`.
:::

:::tip[Keyboard first]
Press :kbd[Ctrl+Shift+P] in the desktop app to open the command palette.
:::

:::warning{collapsible}
This one is collapsible. The body stays hidden until the reader opens it.
:::

## Layout

::::columns
:::column
:::card[Fast]{icon=⚡}
Parses a megabyte of MarkUP in a fraction of a second.
:::
:::
:::column
:::card[Safe]{icon=🛡️}
No raw HTML, and unsafe URLs never reach the output.
:::
:::
:::column
:::card[Extensible]{icon=🧩}
New components are plugins — the parser never changes.
:::
:::
::::

::::tabs
:::tab[npm]
```sh
npm install --global @markup-lang/cli
```
:::
:::tab[From source]
```sh
git clone https://github.com/arturjoaodaros-dev/MarkUP
cd MarkUP && npm install && npm run build
```
:::
::::

