## Text

> MarkUP keeps Markdown readable as plain text.
> Components read like what they are.

1. Write in any editor.
2. Check it with `markup check`.
3. Build it with `markup build`.

- [x] Parser
- [x] Renderers
- [ ] World domination

:::details[What about raw HTML?]
MarkUP deliberately has no raw HTML: `<div>` is shown as text. This keeps documents
portable across renderers and makes previews safe. Use :abbr[CSS]{title="Cascading Style Sheets"} classes on components instead.
:::

```ts {title="render.ts"}
import { markupToHtml } from '@markup-lang/html';

const { html, diagnostics } = markupToHtml('# Hello');
```

[^why]: Footnotes are collected at the end of the document, with links back to each reference.
